  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A bar magnet is passing through a conducting loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The radius of the bar magnet is such that it just passes through the loop. The induced e.m.f. in the loop can be represented by the approximate curve:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c88b273c-a99c-4166-b77e-5bfdacc51392-image.png\" style=\"width: 102px; height: 161px;\" />&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6afea83f-af2a-4000-a59f-fd8f0e28909f-b2909a94-b955-4119-8168-9f16585efe92-image.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 194px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
